==English==

===Etymology===
A contracted form of {{m|en|one's}} {{m|en|self}}. Equivalent to {{suffix|en|one|self}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/wʌnˈsɛlf/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-oneself.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛlf|s=2}}

===Pronoun===
{{en-pron|reflexive form of the indefinite personal pronoun|one|formerly sometimes two words:|one's self}}

# A person's [[self]]: general form of {{m|en|himself}}, {{m|en|herself}}, {{m|en|themself}} or {{m|en|yourself}}.
#: {{ux|en|Teaching '''oneself''' to swim can be dangerous.}}

====Usage notes====
This pronoun can be used for [[emphasis]] or to make a verb [[reflexive]].

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|one's self}}

